A slice is a dynamically sized view into an underlying container. Unlike arrays, which have a strict, fixed length, slices can grow and shrink.

A slice is specified using the `[]` prefix without a size. In this example, the function `Main` returns both an array (type: `[2]int64`) and a slice (type `[]int64`).

```code:main
package main

func newArray() [2]int64 {
    return [2]int64{1, 2}
}

func newSlice() []int64 {
    return []int64{3, 4}
}

func Main() ([2]int64, []int64) {
    return newArray(), newSlice()
}
```

